## How To Work Here

- Make new projects under `/home/{{USERNAME}}/projects` unless the user gives a different location.
- Create the project directory if it does not exist.
- Prefer the toolchain already installed on this box before adding new tools.
- For GitHub work, use the GitHub CLI (`gh`) when possible.
- Before changing a repo, inspect its existing README, package files, task runner, tests, and local conventions.
- Run the smallest useful verification after changes. If you cannot verify something, tell the user what remains unverified.
- Do not expose secrets in chat, logs, commits, screenshots, or generated files.
- Ask the user before destructive actions, force pushes, deleting data, changing billing/account settings, or widening public access.

